> way. And how do you imagine shafts of light and mist, especially in ASCII?
>

A skeleton would look like %.  A sarcophagus would look like (.  Rubble
would look like *.  Broken arrows would look like ).  Shafts of light
would be represented by small illuminated areas on otherwise dark
levels.  Mist would be represented by a "level sound" in which you
comment to yourself that it is misty in here and also by reduced
visibility. ie. your vision radius would be equivalent to that of
carrying a lamp on a dark level, even if you are not carrying a lamp
and the level is not dark. And if the level was dark, then carrying a
lit lamp would not improve your vision radius.  Incidentally, I suppose
broken arrows might be mended with a ?oEW.

